      "systemData": "Physical load: moderate\nCognitive load: moderate\nOrganisational load: moderate\nStudent independence: medium–high",
      "teacherSummary": "3 minutes for goal and safety; 7 minutes for gradual warm-up.\n10 minutes to learn the quality measure and choose a level.\n12 minutes of multi-round practice with one adjustment.\n8-minute applied challenge with no performance ranking.\n5 minutes for reflection, recovery, and orderly collection.",
      "pedagogicalValue": "Why is it important? Cardiorespiratory endurance is among the fitness components most strongly linked to long-term health, and the talk test is the one way to train it that needs no equipment and works for every student in the room.\nWhat does it develop? The ability to hold a moderate intensity over time rather than in bursts, honest self-report even when it means choosing an easier option, and decision-making about effort while already fatigued.\nWhy not skip it? Continuous aerobic work is the component most often dropped because it is unpopular; taught with self-chosen options and the talk test it becomes something every student can succeed at, rather than a run that simply sorts the class by speed.",
