        "mainA": "Duration: 10 minutes. Purpose: learn the central quality marker and choice.\nProcedure: The teacher presents three possible goals: movement quality, consistent pace, or recovery. Each student chooses one goal, one measure, and one familiar station, then writes a success criterion that can be observed.\nOrganisation: pairs; performer and observer switch every minute.\nTeaching points: One goal; one measure; factual feedback; one small change; compare only with yourself.\nCommon errors: starting too fast, holding breath, and feedback that does not name evidence.",
