      "systemData": "Physical load: moderate\nCognitive load: moderate\nOrganisational load: moderate\nStudent independence: medium–high",
      "teacherSummary": "3 minutes for goal and safety; 7 minutes for gradual warm-up.\n10 minutes to learn the quality measure and choose a level.\n12 minutes of multi-round practice with one adjustment.\n8-minute applied challenge with no performance ranking.\n5 minutes for reflection, recovery, and orderly collection.",
      "pedagogicalValue": "Why is it important? It is where fitness stops being something done to students and becomes something they direct: a goal they chose, a measure they named, and a partner coaching them against it.\nWhat does it develop? Writing an observable success criterion, coaching language grounded in evidence rather than encouragement, systematic one-variable revision, and the habit of measuring progress against oneself.\nWhy not skip it? Without a plan of their own, students finish a fitness unit fitter but no more able to train independently; the goal-setting and coaching cycle is the part that transfers beyond the ten lessons.",
