      "assessment": "Teacher checks: choice, technique, regulation, safety, and evidence-based explanation.\nSuccess: plans, performs safely, adjusts one variable, and explains why.\nPartial success: performs safely but needs a prompt to choose or explain.\nNot yet successful: continues despite risk cues, loses spacing, or cannot perform the foundation version after adaptation; stop and return to individual instruction.",
      "reflection": "Teacher questions: Who selected a suitable load? Who changed in response to evidence? Were transitions and work–recovery ratios safe?\nStudent questions: What did you plan? What happened? Which adjustment will you retain?\nNext improvement: change one station, one timing ratio, or one feedback prompt before an individual extension unit or targeted return based on assessment evidence.",
